cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. This is a
  software citation: no paper describing MOTAR has been published, so there is
  no preferred-citation entry. Add one here when a paper exists.
title: "MOTAR: perception, safety-filter analysis, and moving-target rendezvous in simulation"
abstract: >-
  Simulation-only research records covering moving-target tracking,
  dense-obstacle navigation, measured perception error and safety-filter diagnosis,
  together with independent static graphics and reproducibility tools.
  Historical interception experiments and their original capture metrics remain
  explicitly identified; rendezvous terminology does not redefine those results.
  No real-flight result, contact-system validation or deployment is claimed.
type: software
authors:
  # The repository records a GitHub handle and an email for its author and
  # nothing more. A legal name and an ORCID are NOT recorded anywhere in this
  # repository, so they are deliberately left out rather than guessed; add them
  # here when you want them in the citation. Verified from `git log` and the
  # origin remote, both of which agree.
  - name: "joshualikaist"
    email: "kaist.mesc@gmail.com"
    website: "https://github.com/joshualikaist"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshualikaist/MOTAR"
url: "https://github.com/joshualikaist/MOTAR"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
  - simulation
  - perception
  - safety filter
  - reproducibility
date-released: "2026-09-12"
references:
  # MOTAR is a fork of Aerial Gym Simulator and adapts ideas from NavRL. Cite
  # those separately; see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the full component list.
  - type: software
    title: "Aerial Gym Simulator"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/ntnu-arl/aerial_gym_simulator"
    authors:
      - name: "Autonomous Robots Lab, Norwegian University of Science and Technology"
    license: BSD-3-Clause
  - type: software
    title: "rl_games"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Denys88/rl_games"
    authors:
      - name: "Denys Makoviichuk and contributors"
    license: MIT
  - type: software
    title: "NavRL"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Zhefan-Xu/NavRL"
    license: MIT
    authors:
      - name: "Zhefan Xu and contributors"
